{%- comment -%}
  SPADRA V2 product detail page.
  Renders sections B-F of the product spec beneath the stock hero:
    B. The Problem      C. The Solution      D. What's Inside
    E. 30-60-90 Day Protocol Plan            F. You May Also Like
  Content sources:
    - Problem / Benefit / Solution parsed out of product.description
    - spadra.components   -> What's Inside
    - spadra.protocol_90  -> per-phase, product-specific example
    - spadra.related      -> category cross-sells (overridden by quiz matches client-side)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign filt = product.metafields.spadra.filter.value | default: 'all'
  assign comps = product.metafields.spadra.components.value
  assign proto = product.metafields.spadra.protocol_90.value
  assign related = product.metafields.spadra.related.value

  assign desc = product.description
  assign problem = ''
  assign benefit = ''
  assign solution = ''

  assign chunks = desc | split: 'The Problem</strong>'
  if chunks.size > 1
    assign problem = chunks[1] | split: '</p>' | first
  endif
  assign chunks = desc | split: 'The Benefit</strong>'
  if chunks.size > 1
    assign benefit = chunks[1] | split: '</p>' | first
  endif
  assign chunks = desc | split: 'The Solution</strong>'
  if chunks.size > 1
    assign solution = chunks[1] | split: '</p>' | first
  endif

  assign problem = problem | replace: '<br />', '' | replace: '<br/>', '' | replace: '<br>', '' | strip
  assign benefit = benefit | replace: '<br />', '' | replace: '<br/>', '' | replace: '<br>', '' | strip
  assign solution = solution | replace: '<br />', '' | replace: '<br/>', '' | replace: '<br>', '' | strip

  if solution == blank
    assign solution = product.metafields.spadra.science.value
  endif
-%}

{%- liquid
  case filt
  when 'glp1-care'
    assign o1 = 'Establish tolerance and a consistent daily rhythm.'
    assign e1 = 'Most people notice digestive comfort settling first. The goal in month one is not transformation, it is adherence: taking the pouch at the same time daily so absorption becomes predictable alongside your GLP-1 schedule.'
    assign o2 = 'Let nutrient status and metabolic signaling normalize.'
    assign e2 = 'By month two the slower-acting micronutrients reach steadier tissue levels. Energy through the afternoon typically becomes less volatile as glucose handling and nutrient repletion catch up with reduced food intake.'
    assign o3 = 'Reassess body composition and decide the next phase.'
    assign e3 = 'A full quarter is the point where lean-mass preservation and nutrient adequacy can be judged honestly. Review how appetite, energy, and strength have tracked, then keep, adjust, or stack accordingly.'
  when 'focus-brain'
    assign o1 = 'Stabilize the daily baseline before expecting sharpness.'
    assign e1 = 'Calming and precursor ingredients act quickly, so the first change is usually a smoother stress response rather than dramatic cognitive lift. Consistency at the same time each day matters more than dose size.'
    assign o2 = 'Build the neural infrastructure that sustains focus.'
    assign e2 = 'Neurotrophic and mitochondrial ingredients need weeks of continuous presence. Month two is when working memory and afternoon stamina typically feel less effortful to maintain.'
    assign o3 = 'Consolidate the gains into a durable cognitive baseline.'
    assign e3 = 'By the end of the quarter the difference is usually judged by what stopped happening — fewer crashes, less mental static — rather than by a single dramatic moment.'
  when 'bedroom-performance'
    assign o1 = 'Prime the nitric oxide pathway and establish consistency.'
    assign e1 = 'Nitric oxide substrate acts quickly and is often noticed within the first weeks, but the effect is dose-dependent on consistent daily saturation rather than occasional use.'
    assign o2 = 'Let vascular tone and hormonal signaling compound.'
    assign e2 = 'Month two is where endothelial responsiveness and the slower hormonal precursors begin working together, which is when responsiveness typically feels more reliable than situational.'
    assign o3 = 'Evaluate sustained vascular and hormonal baseline.'
    assign e3 = 'A quarter of consistent daily intake is the honest window for judging circulation, stamina, and drive as a baseline rather than a one-off.'
  when 'longevity-beauty'
    assign o1 = 'Saturate the antioxidant and hydration substrate.'
    assign e1 = 'Visible change is rare this early — skin and hair are downstream of cellular processes with long turnover cycles. The first month is about establishing consistent nutrient presence.'
    assign o2 = 'Support the cell turnover cycle already underway.'
    assign e2 = 'Skin renews on roughly a 28-40 day cycle and hair follicles cycle far more slowly. Month two is typically when hydration and clarity changes start becoming noticeable in the mirror.'
    assign o3 = 'Judge structural change on its real timeline.'
    assign e3 = 'Hair density and dermal matrix changes need a full growth-cycle window. Ninety days is the first fair checkpoint, and photographs taken at day one are far more reliable than memory.'
  when 'detox-recovery'
    assign o1 = 'Open and support the clearance pathways.'
    assign e1 = 'Binders and hepatic support act relatively quickly. Some people notice digestion and morning clarity shifting first as elimination becomes more regular.'
    assign o2 = 'Rebuild the antioxidant reserves clearance consumes.'
    assign e2 = 'Glutathione and antioxidant status take weeks to rebuild. Month two is where the burden of ongoing exposure typically starts feeling less cumulative.'
    assign o3 = 'Assess baseline resilience, not a one-time cleanse.'
    assign e3 = 'Detoxification is continuous, not an event. The quarter mark is where you judge whether your everyday baseline — energy, digestion, clarity — has moved.'
  when 'mens-womens-health'
    assign o1 = 'Begin hormonal support without expecting fast change.'
    assign e1 = 'Hormone precursors and metabolism modulators work on endocrine timelines, not daily ones. Month one is foundation: consistent intake and, where relevant, tracking your cycle or symptoms.'
    assign o2 = 'Allow one to two full endocrine cycles to complete.'
    assign e2 = 'Meaningful hormonal shifts require at least one complete cycle, often two. Month two is the earliest honest checkpoint for changes in mood, cycle regularity, or drive.'
    assign o3 = 'Review across a full quarter with your provider.'
    assign e3 = 'Three months spans multiple cycles and is the standard window clinicians use to assess hormonal support. Bring your notes to your provider before extending or adjusting.'
  when 'immune-structural'
    assign o1 = 'Close the nutrient gaps defense and structure depend on.'
    assign e1 = 'Immune and structural tissue rely on cofactors that must first be repleted. Month one is largely invisible work — filling stores before function can improve.'
    assign o2 = 'Let repleted cofactors translate into function.'
    assign e2 = 'Once mineral and vitamin status normalizes, the downstream processes — barrier integrity, immune signaling, tissue maintenance — have what they need to operate.'
    assign o3 = 'Measure resilience over a season, not a week.'
    assign e3 = 'Structural tissue remodels slowly and immune resilience is judged across exposure over time. A quarter is the minimum meaningful window.'
  else
    assign o1 = 'Establish a consistent daily rhythm.'
    assign e1 = 'Month one is about adherence. Taking the pouch at the same time each day is what makes everything that follows measurable.'
    assign o2 = 'Let the slower-acting ingredients reach steady levels.'
    assign e2 = 'Nutrient status normalizes gradually. Month two is typically where day-to-day consistency starts to feel less effortful.'
    assign o3 = 'Reassess against a full quarter of data.'
    assign e3 = 'Ninety days is the first honest checkpoint. Review how you have actually tracked, then keep, adjust, or stack accordingly.'
  endcase
-%}

<section class="spadra-pdp" data-spadra-pdp data-handle="{{ product.handle }}">
  <div class="spadra-pdp__inner">

    {%- if problem != blank -%}
      <div class="spadra-pdp__block spadra-pdp__block--problem">
        <p class="spadra-pdp__eyebrow">The Problem</p>
        <h2 class="spadra-pdp__h2">What this protocol is built to address</h2>
        <p class="spadra-pdp__lede">{{ problem }}</p>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if solution != blank -%}
      <div class="spadra-pdp__block spadra-pdp__block--solution">
        <p class="spadra-pdp__eyebrow">The Solution</p>
        <h2 class="spadra-pdp__h2">How {{ product.title }} works</h2>
        {%- if benefit != blank -%}
          <p class="spadra-pdp__callout">{{ benefit }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <p class="spadra-pdp__body">{{ solution }}</p>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if comps and comps.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="spadra-pdp__block spadra-pdp__block--inside">
        <p class="spadra-pdp__eyebrow">What's Inside</p>
        <h2 class="spadra-pdp__h2">{{ comps.size }} active{% if comps.size != 1 %}s{% endif %}, pre-sorted into one daily pouch</h2>
        <ul class="spadra-ing-list">
          {%- for c in comps -%}
            {%- liquid
              case c
                when 'Theanine'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports alpha-wave calm without sedation.'
                when 'Tyrosine'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports dopamine and norepinephrine precursor supply.'
                when 'Rhodiola'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports adaptogenic buffering of the stress response.'
                when 'Ashwagandha'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports cortisol regulation under sustained load.'
                when 'Ginger Root'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports settling of gastric irritation and nausea signaling.'
                when 'Melatonin SR'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports circadian re-synchronization.'
                when 'Herbal Sleep Blend'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'GABAergic wind-down support.'
                when 'Magnesium'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports muscular relaxation and NMDA-receptor calming.'
                when 'Creatine'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports phosphocreatine reloading for rapid ATP turnover.'
                when 'BCAA'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports amino substrate for muscle protein synthesis.'
                when 'Citrulline'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports nitric oxide substrate delivery.'
                when 'Arginine'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports endothelial nitric oxide production.'
                when 'Big Libido'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Botanical libido support.'
                when 'Taurine'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports neurotransmitter and hydration rebalancing.'
                when 'Green Coffee Extract'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Chlorogenic acid support for fatty-acid oxidation.'
                when 'Soothing Fiber'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports gentle binding and transit regulation.'
                when 'Triphala'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Overnight evacuation support.'
                when 'Glutamine'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports tight-junction repair along the gut wall.'
                when 'Forslean'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Cyclic-AMP signaling support.'
                when 'Methyl B-Complex'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports bioactive B-vitamin cofactor repletion.'
                when 'Vitamin C'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports antioxidant recycling and collagen cofactor supply.'
                when 'NAC'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports glutathione precursor loading.'
                when 'Quercetin'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports mast-cell stabilization and inflammatory damping.'
                when '10B Probiotic'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports microbial diversity rebuilding.'
                when 'Milk Thistle'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports hepatocyte membrane stabilization.'
                when 'Alpha Lipoic Acid'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports intracellular antioxidant regeneration.'
                when 'Turmeric'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports inflammatory signaling downregulation.'
                when 'Green Tea Extract'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports catechin-driven antioxidant defense.'
                when 'Cordyceps'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports oxygen-utilization efficiency.'
                when 'Berberine 500'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports AMPK activation for glucose disposal.'
                when 'Chromium'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Insulin-receptor sensitivity support.'
                when 'Carnitine'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports fatty-acid transport into mitochondria.'
                when 'CoQ10'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports electron-transport chain efficiency.'
                when 'Multivitamin'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports broad micronutrient gap closure.'
                when 'Mushroom Immune'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports beta-glucan immune priming.'
                when 'Omega 3'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports cell-membrane fluidity and resolution of inflammation.'
                when "Lion's Mane"
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports nerve growth factor expression.'
                when 'NR'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports NAD+ pool replenishment.'
                when 'Resveratrol'
                  assign ing_benefit = 'Supports sirtuin pathway activation.'
                when 'Zinc'
